tures, xslt-v3-fixtures,\nbuild-file-host-profiles, v3-tag-vocab-extend, shell-rc-host-carriers, dockerfile-multistage-stage-graph,\ncorpus-aggregate-questions.\nRead with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n  D18 solve.py and in lib.codec since D18 night). **D19 broke the raw-bytes assumption**: the ASPX host carries the whole\n  inner script as an escaped string literal (`\\n`, `\\\"`), so marker data runs into `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is\n  `\\\"`-quoted (lib.codec.v3_plan handles it; the carried solve.py needed a patch). D20 had no carrier twist. The real D21+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n  -- yet (nor D19-D21's). D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1211439-e94b-4837-908f-ec92ba91c12b","uuid":"0e09f80d-a6c0-4cb5-820a-27549769663a","timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:04:37.260Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"297 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md\n1:# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D28 seen vs. D29+ candidates)\n80:## 1. Concept table\n193:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n253:## Readiness gaps\n# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D28 seen vs. D29+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-28 after D28 (single 1703 ids = +44, 179 members; \"Out of Order\" / base `terraform-cloud-timeline` added 4\n`polyglot-terraform_hcl-*.tf`, NO host, no new bash -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `terraform { required_version =\n\">= 1.0\" }`, `locals { huntress_descriptor_<8hex> = \"<data>\" }`, `output \"inert_analysis_<8hex>\" { value =\nlocal.huntress_descriptor_<8hex> }`; no resources/providers/depends_on/timestamps). Carried D23 solver answered everything\nunpatched: single CORRECT ~T+49 s (race win, 0 wrong), TT 1781 and Mastery (**12 sets**, 21372) first try. **The timed contract\nflipped BACK to the per-file grammar** (D23-D26 shape: `<family>-<6hex>-<field>